profile forge.world.core.v1

; ORTHOGONAL PERSISTENCE — its OWN slow clock domain (every 3): the rotor persists between ticks without the
; locus asking to be saved; where the state physically lives between epochs is the runtime's business.
[pulser:op_clock](every 3){sig_out}
[spinner:op_locus](w=16, n=8, rotor=quarter_turn_z){sig_in, socket}
[orb:op_view]{pose}

[op_clock] --sig--> [op_locus]
[op_locus] --socket--> [op_view]
